			<div class="content" id="post-content-3206040">
									

<p>Do you notice the space you walk through every day?<br />
Have you ever felt like there was an itch inside your head?<br />
Do you ever think about what is going on there, deep inside, where you can't go or even see?</p>
<p>This is a story about how the Foundation doesn't always know why things happen. It is kind of a thematic sequel to SCP-2365.</p>
<p>Many thanks to MrWrong for feedback on the forums. The image is from Wikipedia <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leatherback_sea_turtle#/media/File:Leatherback_turtle_oesophagus.jpg">here</a>, by mdomingoa, and is on a CC-by-SA 4.0 licence.</p>
<p>ETA: if you came here from the features page, and enjoyed this, why not check out my other SCPs and tales. You can find them at <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/psuls-author-page">my author page</a>.</p>

